From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hannes Janetzek <hannes.janetzek@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 21:35:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Make all directories configurable through environment
 variables

New zynconf/zynthian_paths.py computes every directory once: each can be
set with its ZYNTHIAN_*_DIR variable, unset ones derive from ZYNTHIAN_DIR
(default "/zynthian", the ZynthianOS layout) and ZYNTHIAN_UI_DIR defaults
to the directory the code runs from. The values are written back to
os.environ, so code reading the variables directly and child processes
see the same.

Replace the hardcoded "/zynthian/..." paths and the scattered
os.environ.get() defaults with it. On ZynthianOS nothing changes.

zynthian_lv2.py adds the UI directory to sys.path when run as a script
(first boot), so it can import zynconf.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit ede9c3fc5f41b72143c663ab51bb946b44499053)
